38 #edb/ref 17592186400694 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186124483 1038 #edb/ref 17592186400526 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186124483 1038 #edb/ref 17592186400533 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186124483 1038 #edb/ref 17592186400540 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186124484 1038 #edb/ref 17592186400547 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186124484 1038 #edb/ref 17592186400554 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186124486 1038 #edb/ref 17592186400596 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186124550 1038 #edb/ref 17592186400736 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186129166 1038 #edb/ref 17592186400722 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186129166 1038 #edb/ref 17592186400729 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186129487 1068 #edb/ref 17592186126392 13194139533482 17592186045585 false] [17592186129487 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400743 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186129487 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186129487 1071 "A particle moves with a constant acceleration of $(3i + 2j)m/s^{2}$. The velocity of the particle is $(-7i - 6j)m/s$ when $t = 0s$. Find the time when the velocity of the particle equals $2im/s$." 13194139533482 17592186045585 false] [17592186129487 1071 "A particle moves with a constant acceleration of $(3i+2j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$ The velocity of the particle is $(-7i-6j)\\,\\text{m/s}$ when $t=0\\,\\text{s}.$ Find the time when the velocity of the particle equals $2i\\,\\text{m/s}.$" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186129487 1074 "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nv=u+at,\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is the initial velocity, and $a$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\na=3i+2j,\\,u=-7i-6j,\\,v=2i\n$$\n\ninto the equation above, we can solve for $t,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\ 2i & =(-7i-6j)+(3i+2j)t \\\\ 9i+6j & =(3i+2j)t \\\\ 9i+6j & =3ti+2tj\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the $i$ and $j$ components in the last equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}9=3t \\\\ 6=2t\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,t=3\\,\\text{s}.\n$$" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186152175 1038 #edb/ref 17592186400568 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186152175 1038 #edb/ref 17592186400575 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186152282 1038 #edb/ref 17592186400561 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186161971 1038 #edb/ref 17592186400484 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186161972 1038 #edb/ref 17592186400498 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186161973 1038 #edb/ref 17592186400477 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186179660 1038 #edb/ref 17592186400701 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186229143 1038 #edb/ref 17592186400470 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400470 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400471 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400470 1069 "q-130261" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400470 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400470 1071 "Which of the following are linear differential operators?\n\nI. ${D}_{1}(y)=x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-2xy$\nII. ${D}_{2}(y)={x}^{3}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}$\nIII. ${D}_{3}(y)=y\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+xy$" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400470 1072 #uuid "3d8c3559-a0d3-57b0-8496-a5eb629e4fde" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400470 1074 "For any linear differential operator,\n\n$$\nD(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})=aD({y}_{1})+bD({y}_{2})\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants. \n\nLet's check each case in turn.\n\n- The first operator is indeed linear. To see this, we check the above linearity condition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{1}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) & =x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})-2x(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) \\\\  & =ax\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+bx\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-2ax{y}_{1}-2bx{y}_{2} \\\\  & =a[x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-2x{y}_{1}]+b[x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-2x{y}_{2}] \\\\  & =a{D}_{1}({y}_{1})+b{D}_{1}({y}_{2})\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second operator is also linear. To see this, we check the above linearity condition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{2}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) & ={x}^{3}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) \\\\  & =a{x}^{3}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+b{x}^{3}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =a[{x}^{3}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}]+b[{x}^{3}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}] \\\\  & =a{D}_{2}({y}_{1})+b{D}_{2}({y}_{2})\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The third operator is **not** linear.\nTo see why, we first evaluate the left-hand side of the linearity condition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{3}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) & =(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})+x(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2}) \\\\  & =(a{y}_{1}+b{y}_{2})(a\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+b\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}})+ax{y}_{1}+bx{y}_{2} \\\\  & ={a}^{2}{y}_{1}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{b}^{2}{y}_{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+ab({y}_{1}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{y}_{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}})+ax{y}_{1}+bx{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is not the same as the right-hand side, because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a{D}_{3}({y}_{1})+b{D}_{3}({y}_{2}) & =a[{y}_{1}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+x{y}_{1}]+b[{y}_{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+x{y}_{2}] \\\\  & =a{y}_{1}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{1}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+b{y}_{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+ax{y}_{1}+bx{y}_{2}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400471 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400472 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400471 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400473 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400471 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400474 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400471 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400475 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400471 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400476 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400471 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400471 1077 "selection" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400471 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400475 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400471 1080 #uuid "c0b85420-0caa-5a47-aa4b-176ffc8735f4" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400472 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400472 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400472 1084 #uuid "c50bae7c-4e9f-5360-a509-ff44725d8a45" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400473 1081 "I only" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400473 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400473 1084 #uuid "180930f4-6ef0-5699-aaf0-df74299a4406" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400474 1081 "III only" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400474 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400474 1084 #uuid "dd59af1e-9a02-50a6-a868-999451ea5ac3" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400475 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400475 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400475 1084 #uuid "29fac9c5-fa11-5337-b426-2051164249e3" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400476 1081 "II only" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400476 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400476 1084 #uuid "5975f4ce-bb96-58c1-b253-172e6c5a0d8f" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400477 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400478 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400477 1069 "q-130448" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400477 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400477 1071 "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 8 & -7 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 11 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary row operations of the form ${R}_{i}:={R}_{i}+k{R}_{1},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary row operations?" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400477 1072 #uuid "fc4fe478-ecca-5d83-9a4b-47e34a0bc1c8" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400477 1074 "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries below ${a}_{12}=-2$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 8 & -7 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 11 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 11 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}.$" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400478 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400479 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400478 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400480 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400478 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400481 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400478 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400482 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400478 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400483 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400478 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400478 1077 "selection" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400478 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400483 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400478 1080 #uuid "1ddf9b10-51fd-5a37-b528-b67408ad0ada" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400479 1081 "${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-{R}_{1}$" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400479 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400479 1084 #uuid "5a7281f6-7e60-5d96-9073-2b79663c148b" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400480 1081 "${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-{R}_{1}$" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400480 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400480 1084 #uuid "3d1c46db-e09e-574c-8457-d835d0d60cb8" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400481 1081 "${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1}$" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400481 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400481 1084 #uuid "909cb4b3-d84a-5df3-b043-02b797c8f6d7" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400482 1081 "${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}$" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400482 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400482 1084 #uuid "496f929c-182e-536d-8240-53d72e20d1ef" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400483 1081 "${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}$" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400483 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400483 1084 #uuid "1e501008-96e1-5873-9523-2270ec047af7" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400484 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400485 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400484 1069 "q-130462" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400484 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533482