139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400505 1071 "Which of the following are elementary matrices?\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,Q=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,S=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400505 1072 #uuid "0d49dd3c-2d26-5daf-baa6-13e98e158d10" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400505 1074 "An elementary matrix is a matrix obtained from the identity matrix by applying exactly one elementary row operation. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- The matrices $P$ and $Q$ are not elementary matrices because they can't be obtained from ${I}_{2}$ by applying only one elementary row operation.\n\n- The matrix $S$ is an elementary matrix because it can be obtained from ${I}_{2}$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =S\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $S$ is an elementary matrix." 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400506 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400507 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400506 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400508 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400506 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400509 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400506 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400510 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400506 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400511 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400506 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400506 1077 "selection" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400506 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400507 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400506 1080 #uuid "ce429fdf-6b6f-5359-bf73-1a833c32c68d" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400507 1081 "$S$ only" 13194139533482 1