s examine our matrices.\n\n- The matrices $A$ and $C$ are not elementary matrices because they can't be obtained from ${I}_{2}$ by applying only one elementary row operation.\n\n- The matrix $B$ is an elementary matrix because it can be obtained from ${I}_{2}$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:=4{R}_{1},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{1}:=4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $B$ is an elementary matrix." 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400513 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400514 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400513 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400515 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400513 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400516 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400513 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400517 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400513 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400518 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400513 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400513 1077 "selection" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400513 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400517 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400513 1080 #uuid "70925ade-385f-5362-ac6e-a022a4d19eae" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400514 1081 "$A$  only" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400514 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400514 1084 #uuid "1494e45b-e9c6-535d-9eba-3790fc3b3525" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400515 1081 "$C$  only" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400515 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400515 1084 #uuid "9c2aeafd-d65d-5e22-bb2e-c7f378129297" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400516 1081 "$A$  and $B$ only" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400516 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400516 1084 #uuid "15a62809-c816-544c-b95c-2f003c843342" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400517 1081 "$B$  only" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400517 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400517 1084 #uuid "97c97b06-f6db-546d-aa97-0f3a35c8b667" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400518 1081 "$A$  and $C$ only" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400518 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400518 1084 #uuid "164d8bbe-3777-525f-8440-8bfe402f43f4" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400519 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400520 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400519 1069 "q-130927" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400519 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400519 1071 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+2y-z=4 \\\\  & -3x-6y+4z=-8 \\\\  & 3x+7y-z=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400519 1072 #uuid "8eff9d12-5ab8-5d85-973e-0e821294f176" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400519 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -3 & -6 & 4 & -8 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -1 & 10\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -3 & -6 & 4 & -8 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -1 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 7 & -1 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y-z=4 \\\\ y+2z=-2 \\\\ z=4,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=4$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+2(4)=-2\\,⟹\\,y=-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $y=-10$ and $z=4$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2(-10)-(4)=4\\,⟹\\,x=28.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=28$, $y=-10$, and $z=4.$" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400520 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400521 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400520 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400522 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400520 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400523 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400520 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400524 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400520 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400525 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400520 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400520 1077 "selection" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400520 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400522 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400520 1080 #uuid "924e4677-652c-5aa5-ad82-4e9a728fb938" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400521 1081 "$x=-12$, $y=6$, and $z=-4$" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400521 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400521 1084 #uuid "29e0739b-acd3-5213-baab-e978002551c4" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400522 1081 "$x=28$, $y=-10$, and $z=4$" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400522 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400522 1084 #uuid "09aec1aa-dcc4-5694-820b