his matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -9 & -3 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -9 & -3 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x,$ and we have two free variables, $y$ and $z.$ That means we can find $x$ in terms of $y$ and $z.$ \n\nTherefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*. \n\nAs a result, only statement III is true." 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400639 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400640 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400639 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400641 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400639 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400642 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400639 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400643 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400639 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400644 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400639 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400639 1077 "selection" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400639 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400642 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400639 1080 #uuid "97478289-921c-5024-949c-f21308c68969" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400640 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400640 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400640 1084 #uuid "461eef6c-aefb-5663-8d03-db54f697d105" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400641 1081 "I only" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400641 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400641 1084 #uuid "b3d3c662-b67b-5b81-a307-d2b8efde6388" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400642 1081 "III only" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400642 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400642 1084 #uuid "fbcd7fd9-5df8-5756-a9f3-48cc31c9e67e" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400643 1081 "None" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400643 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400643 1084 #uuid "ec9dcc22-2e73-56c0-825d-9e630c431eb4" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400644 1081 "II only" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400644 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400644 1084 #uuid "56e99c2d-29cc-5ded-a5f5-80ae572f982d" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400645 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400646 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400645 1069 "q-131721" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400645 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400645 1071 "Consider the following system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+2y=-1 \\\\  & 3x+7y=1 \\\\  & -2x-4y=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The system is consistent independent\nII. The system has no solution\nIII. The system is consistent dependent" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400645 1072 #uuid "b9b47374-5548-52b6-9b51-17d923fcd37b" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400645 1074 "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 7 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ are solutions to the third equation $0x+0y=0$, we can remove this equation from the system. So, the corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y=-1 \\\\ y=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation we have $y=4$ and substituting this into the first equation yields $x=-9.$ So,  we conclude that the system is consistent independent. \n\nAs a result, only statement I is true." 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400646 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400647 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400646 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400648 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400646 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400649 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400646 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400650 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400646 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400651 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400646 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400646 1077 "selection" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400646 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400648 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400646 1080 #uuid "62ec4d2b-adce-53b9-bdc4-0b08d9bbcf9a" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400647 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400647 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400647 1084 #uuid "baed0cbf-38ec-5d81-9809-43dafa9379a2" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400648 1081 "I only" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400648 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400648 1084 #uuid "586150d0-53a3-501e-a821-68c180a394cd" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400649 1081 "III only" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400649 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400649 1084 #uuid "a39c1a3e-21c9-5508-8921-b8a05957b672" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400650 1081 "None" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400650 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400650 1084 #uuid "2247b748-8cef-53eb-82f9-2487685f5057" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400651 1081 "II only" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400651 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400651 1084 #uuid "77d955a7-8c55-5d69-9764-f442198cee4b" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400652 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400653 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400652 1069 "q-131722" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400652 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400652 1071 "Consider the following system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 3x-3y=6 \\\\  & -2x+y=-3 \\\\  & 4x-4y=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The system is consistent dependent\nII. The system is consistent independent\nIII. The system has no solution" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400652 1072 #uuid "4890e1ff-ed9a-5558-acd1-bcef01439e04" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400652 1074 "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ are solutions to the third equation $0x+0y=0$, we can remove this equation from the system. So, the corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y=2 \\\\ y=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation we have $y=-1$ and substituting this into the first equation yields $x=1.$ So,  we conclude that the system is consistent independent. \n\nAs a result, only statement II is true." 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400653 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400654 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400653 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400655 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400653 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400656 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400653 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400657 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400653 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400658 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400653 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400653 1077 "selection" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400653 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400658 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400653 1080 #uuid "cb13c3f2-95da-5f1e-8dd8-8f023abfea3e" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400654 1081 "I only" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400654 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400654 1084 #uuid "1c927d7e-5c4b-5882-8721-adc2b5fd92e3" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400655 1081 "III only" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400655 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400655 1084 #uuid "64d69900-4157-5d22-aa0e-f4d914c8f721" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400656 1081 "None" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400656 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400656 1084 #uuid "2aba7c87-fdf8-526c-bf60-804628ebce56" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400657 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400657 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400657 1084 #uuid "fea224bb-b24d-5ae7-9e7c-a1698eef7494" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400658 1081 "II only" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400658 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400658 1084 #uuid "a62e5405-e20d-5e9c-833b-ebb37c50b5ed" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400659 1068 #edb/ref 17592186400660 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400659 1069 "q-132204" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400659 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400659 1071 "Find the center and radius of the osculating circle to the curve $r(t)$ at the point $P(0,0)$ where $t=0,$ given that $‖{r}^{′}(0)‖=1,$ and the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ to the curve is\n\n$$\nT(t)=⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩.\n$$" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400659 1072 #uuid "3e19d212-99bc-5ec6-ba7f-76b0f4f4e8f9" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400659 1074 "Since we are given both the value of $‖{r}^{′}(0)‖$ and the unit tangent $T(t)$, we will use the following formula for the radius of curvature:\n\n$$\nR(t)=\\frac{1}{κ(t)}=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNotice that $r(0)=⟨0,0⟩,$ since the point $P(0,0)$ is at the tip of $r(0).$ \n\nNow, we find ${T}^{′}(t)$, ${T}^{′}(0)$ and $‖{T}^{′}(0)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\ {T}^{′}(0) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡0,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,0⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(0)‖ & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the radius of curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(0) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(0)‖}{‖{T}^{′}(0)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal normal vector at $t=0$ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(0) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(0)}{‖{T}^{′}(0)‖}=⟨1,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the center of the osculating circle is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(0)+R(0)N(0) & =⟨0,0⟩+1\\cdot ⟨1,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,0⟩+⟨1,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400660 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400661 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400660 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400662 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400660 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400663 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400660 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400664 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400660 1075 #edb/ref 17592186400665 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400660 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400660 1077 "selection" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400660 1079 #edb/ref 17592186400661 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400660 1080 #uuid "c7e8d157-633b-58f4-9968-e3a163c79d0d" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400661 1081 "The center is $⟨1,0⟩$ and the radius is $1$" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400661 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400661 1084 #uuid "dc2c4fc2-a754-53f6-ab25-c364e85fb49f" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400662 1081 "The center is $⟨1,1⟩$ and the radius is $1$" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400662 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400662 1084 #uuid "6c3b49b7-2177-58c7-9dfd-a4e06235e607" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400663 1081 "The center is $⟨1,0⟩$ and the radius is $2$" 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400663 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533482 17592186045585 true] [17592186400663 1